hadiths[5]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24256","Ali ibn Abdillah narrated to us, Ibn Wahb narrated to us, Amr ibn al-Harith informed me, from Bakr ibn Suwadah al-Judhami, from Ziyad ibn Nu'aym al-Hadrami, from Amr ibn Hazm, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me leaning on a grave and said: Do not harm the occupant of this grave, or: Do not harm him."
"24257","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Bakr ibn Sawadah, from Ziyad ibn Nu'aym, from Amr ibn Hazm, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me on a grave and said: Come down; do not harm the occupant of this grave. In another place Ziyad ibn Nu'aym said that Ibn Hazm, either Amr or Umarah, said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me on a grave."
"24258","Affan narrated to us, Abd al-Wahid narrated to us, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm narrated to me, from Amr ibn Hazm, who said: I presented, or he said: I presented, the ruqyah of the bite from the snake to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he commanded it."
"24259","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, Ma'mar informed us, from Ibn Tawus, from Abu Bakr ibn Muhammad ibn Amr ibn Hazm, from his father, who said: When Ammar ibn Yasir was killed, Amr ibn Hazm entered upon Amr ibn al-As and said: Ammar has been killed, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The rebellious party will kill him."
"24260","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Abdullah ibn Wahb narrated to us, from Amr, meaning Ibn al-Harith, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hilal, from Abu Bakr ibn Hazm, that al-Nadr ibn Abdillah informed him, from Amr ibn Hazm, that he heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Do not sit on graves."
